From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:45:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayerAudio: drop the rest of a frame when a resync
 flushes

A frame that timed out while being added stays half written and its
rest is added on the next pass. A resync that flushes the sink kept
that rest, so audio from before the flush was played after it, without
a timestamp of its own. The flush and reset messages already drop it.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.cpp
@@ -0,6 +0,7 @@
       if (pts > m_audioClock - delay + 0.5 * DVD_TIME_BASE)
       {
         m_audioSink.Flush();
+        audioframe.nb_frames = 0;
       }
       m_audioClock = pts + delay;
       if (m_speed != DVD_PLAYSPEED_PAUSE)
